Right, looking at these. The ones with no calorie numbers don't do much for me. I'm not working out calories on a Tuesday, but I do look at prices, so a number I can compare feels more useful than a warning. The shocking photos would probably just make me think they're treating me like a kid, the same as the five-a-day posters. A bold number on everything, the healthy stuff included, is the closest to what I'd actually use, because I'd see a Dairy Milk next to a fruit pot and think about it, even if I still bought the Dairy Milk half the time.

