Mostly I'd ignore these. The photos would just annoy me. A bowel tumour on a packet of crisps is the bus-shelter shouting I already can't stand, and I'd be thinking about the price, not the picture. The plain text warnings are a bit better, but I've read "excess calories" on everything since I was a teenager.

The bold calorie numbers on everything are the only thing that would actually change anything. I don't count calories, but seeing 95 next to 240 when I'm standing at the machine hungry and in a rush might make me reach for the fruit pot. Even then, I'd still be weighing up what's left in my purse and whether it's already in the house.

